WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
Two shops each put up their
prices by 10 per cent.

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.870
At the first shop, the
money coming in goes up.

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.970
At the second, it goes down.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.810
Firms setting prices need to
know which result they will get.

5
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.500
So do governments choosing what to tax.

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.950
Revenue is simply price
times quantity sold.

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.940
So when a seller charges more,

8
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.520
why does the money
coming in sometimes go up

9
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.190
and sometimes go down?

10
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll draw the two
rectangles that every price rise creates:

11
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.960
one gained, one lost.

12
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.030
Then you'll move a slider
until the result flips,

13
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.940
and find the tipping point.

14
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: find out what
decides which way the money moves.
